- SSH is the crypto verifier. Strict host checks, no localhost/DNS trust bypass, no control-socket reuse, no forwarding/background/local command. External known_hosts and user-key settings remain SSH-owned. A local privileged operator can replace ssh/config; protection from compromised local accounts is outside Section 16.1.
