- Pipe ownership: parent owns all endpoints until Start; closes child-side copies after Start. One bounded stdout queue, one reader frame, counted/discarded stderr. Close/context/budget/read/exit failures terminate and reap direct process, close pipes, join pumps. Unix uses a process group. Escaping setsid descendants are outside termination scope but cannot keep pipe waits alive; Windows direct child only, native tree termination unclaimed.
- No durable AX mutation or public listener. Crash/idempotency state injection N/A. Repeated Close, cancellation/exit races, failed read recovery and inherited-pipe release use real local processes.
